---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const consoleUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONSOLE_URL || 'http://localhost:3000/login';
const controls = [
  { no: '01', title: 'The model does not write', body: 'An investigator may assemble cited hypotheses and recommendations. Deterministic control modules decide whether an action is permitted.' },
  { no: '02', title: 'A single write path', body: 'The executor is the only caller allowed to initiate a target write. An uncertain outcome is recorded as unknown and reconciled by reading state.' },
  { no: '03', title: 'Approval bound to evidence', body: 'Approval applies to a specific evidence set, report, disposition and policy version. A changed basis requires a new review.' },
  { no: '04', title: 'Verification before closure', body: 'The observed business state must match the expected state. An HTTP success response is not a resolution.' },
  { no: '05', title: 'Audit beside the effect', body: 'Case transitions and consequential decisions append audit events inside their business transaction. Follow-up delivery uses an outbox.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trust model — Action Integrity"
  description="The safety boundaries, accountability rules and release status behind Action Integrity."
  current="trust"
>
  <section class="trust-hero">
    <div class="wrap trust-hero-inner">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">PUBLIC SYSTEM / TRUST MODEL</span><h1>The control boundary is the product.</h1><p>Action Integrity is designed to make a harmful automated decision harder to execute and easier to examine. These are the rules the system must prove, not claims that a polished interface can substitute for.</p></div>
      <div class="hero-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><span>CONTROL<br />BEFORE<br />ACTION</span><small>01 / 05</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="controls">
    <div class="wrap"><div class="section-header"><span class="section-index">01 / SAFETY BOUNDARIES</span><h2 class="section-heading">Five rules across the action lifecycle.</h2></div>
      <div class="control-list">{controls.map((control) => <article><span class="control-no">{control.no}</span><h3>{control.title}</h3><p>{control.body}</p></article>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="accountability">
    <div class="wrap accountability-grid">
      <div><span class="section-index">02 / HUMAN ACCOUNTABILITY</span><h2 class="section-heading">No administrator shortcut to a business decision.</h2></div>
      <div><p>Reviewers approve a disposition against the evidence they saw. Higher-risk actions require distinct people and role coverage. The person taking a post-approval action cannot be one of its approvers.</p><p>Platform administrators manage access and operations. Their platform role alone does not grant approval or execution rights for business actions.</p><a class="text-link" href={consoleUrl}>Inspect the control room <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="release-status">
    <div class="wrap release-grid"><div><span class="section-index">03 / RELEASE STATUS</span><h2 class="section-heading">The implementation is in progress.</h2></div><div class="release-panel"><span class="status-label"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> DEVELOPMENT / DEMO</span><p>This site describes the intended operating model. A release is production-capable only after its automated readiness checks pass on the release commit. Production approval also requires named operational and security sign-offs.</p><p>Until then, the application uses synthetic demonstration data. This page does not claim a certification, zero downtime, full autonomy or approval for real customer data.</p></div></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trust-hero { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--steel); background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 0 79px, rgba(56,46,48,.18) 80px), var(--carbon); }
  .trust-hero-inner { min-height: 410px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr .6fr; gap: 48px; align-items: center; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(42px, 4.2vw, 58px); line-height: 1.07; letter-spacing: -.05em; font-weight: 500; max-width: 760px; margin: 24px 0 20px; }
  .trust-hero p { max-width: 690px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--muted); }
  .hero-stamp { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; width: 230px; height: 230px; border: 1px solid var(--signal); padding: 20px; transform: rotate(-4deg); margin-left: auto; }
  .hero-stamp span { color: var(--signal); font: 29px/1.03 var(--font-mono); }
  .hero-stamp small { align-self: end; color: var(--muted); font: 10px var(--font-mono); }
  .controls, .accountability, .release-status { padding: 88px 0; }
  .section-header { margin-bottom: 45px; }
  .control-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--steel); }
  .control-list article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 70px .8fr 1.2fr; align-items: start; gap: 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--steel); padding: 28px 0; }
  .control-no { color: var(--signal); font: 12px var(--font-mono); padding-top: 5px; }
  .control-list h3 { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 500; margin: 0; }
  .control-list p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; max-width: 550px; }
  .accountability { background: var(--graphite); border-block: 1px solid var(--steel); }
  .accountability-grid, .release-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 64px; }
  .accountability-grid > div:nth-child(2) { padding-top: 28px; }
  .accountability p, .release-panel p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .text-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 35px; margin-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--signal); font-size: 14px; }
  .text-link span { color: var(--signal); }
  .release-panel { background: var(--graphite); border: 1px solid var(--steel); padding: 28px; }
  .status-label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; margin-bottom: 22px; color: var(--warning); font: 11px var(--font-mono); }
  .status-label i { width: 7px; height: 7px; background: var(--warning); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .trust-hero-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; padding: 70px 0; }.hero-stamp { display: none; }.accountability-grid, .release-grid { gap: 40px; }.control-list article { grid-template-columns: 45px 1fr; }.control-list p { grid-column: 2; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .controls, .accountability, .release-status { padding: 70px 0; }.accountability-grid, .release-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 10px; }.control-list article { gap: 10px; }.control-list h3 { font-size: 19px; } }
</style>
